A||||34||Smokin' GT||has anyone had bad experiences with West Coast Fiero?||||13||
Z||000000||Smokin' GT||12-03-2001||04:57 PM||||Just wondering, because their service doesn't seem that great to me.  About 2 1/2 weeks ago I ordered their spin-tech adapted muffler.  Then two weeks later after nothing had came I called them and they didn't know anything about it so they took my order again and said they would send it 2-day air.  That was on wednesday last week, it's now monday and I'm getting pretty pissed.  <P>Has anyone had similar problems or is it just my order?<P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||13
Z||000001||Smokin' GT||12-03-2001||05:20 PM||||nevermind, just showed up!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Mr.Frosty||12-03-2001||05:21 PM||||Dang,and you're in the same state.I wonder how long it would take to go elswhere.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||12-03-2001||05:26 PM||||I have always had great customer service from WCF, on the delivery side.  I will say that if you plan on purchasing their engine mounts, make sure to ask a few questions rather than assuming anything.  I cannot vouch for any of their other parts.  I am a strong supporter of, "You get what you pay for," but this is not true in every case.  Please be sure you know what you are getting before ordering it.<P>I had an issue with Eric from WCF, in which he <B>GAVE</B> me some parts, asking me to let him know my impressions.  I did so, letting him know my opinion of the parts, and was disregarded thereafter.  I had planned on buying more from him (over $1000 worth) and hoped to provide some useful information for his parts development, but like I said, my opinion was disregarded and my business right along with it.  <P>Eric, I am sure this will piss you off, especially with your recent falling out from the forum; I'm just telling it like it is.  Hopefully you are more upset with the situation than me personally, but I can't change how you feel about it.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||12-03-2001||05:51 PM||||my opinion is that the product is very good but the delivery slow.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smokin' GT||12-03-2001||06:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>my opinion is that the product is very good but the delivery slow.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think I read somewhere else that you got a spin-tech too, how does it sound?  I doubt there's little if any performance benefit but did you notice any?<P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||5
Z||000006||FieroLisa||12-03-2001||06:29 PM||||I have the spintech but haven't had it installed...currently I'm a sad 500 miles away from my Fiero, and I've only gotten quotes from one muffler shop for install and they were tryin to tell me it would cost me like $500 or somethin ludicrous like that!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Smokin' GT||12-03-2001||06:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I have the spintech but haven't had it installed...currently I'm a sad 500 miles away from my Fiero, and I've only gotten quotes from one muffler shop for install and they were tryin to tell me it would cost me like $500 or somethin ludicrous like that!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>$500 just to install the muffler or are you going with bigger pipe?  <P>Of the two places I've talked to, the first place said $40, and the other said $65.  This is just for replacing the muffler though...||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||12-03-2001||06:42 PM||||Yah all I WANNA do is replace the muffler. They saw a female driving a fiero and must've mistaken that for a total retard ready to give up 500 bucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||jimmybpei||12-03-2001||06:48 PM||||Lisa- $500 bucks, i would say somebody is smokin something from a pipe. I installed a complete dual exhaust system from the manifolds to the tips on my 4.5 caddy with 2 muffers for 175.00 can. So thats about 110.00 us <P>You should be able to get a muffler shop to put that on for about 30.00 Cash.<P>Good luck and no offense but dont let them push you around thinkin you don't know anything about cars 'cause your a girl...<P>Later.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||12-03-2001||06:50 PM||||Man, don't those muffler shops know us Fiero owner are po!  (can't even afford the entire word, "poor")  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Of course, I'm in willing poverty.  Anytime I get some extra money, it goes into the Fiero.  Man, I love it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Smokin' GT||12-03-2001||06:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Yah all I WANNA do is replace the muffler.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>$500!!  I can only think of one thing... they must have been drunk!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jefrysuko||12-03-2001||06:54 PM||||This is the latest interaction I have had with WCF.  I will let everyone decide if it was good or bad.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015877.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015877.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||chester||12-03-2001||07:54 PM||||I have purchased many a product from West Coast Fiero.  Though their product is good to very good (IMHO) the delivery is VERY lacking.  I have had them quote me an item "in stock" just to find out that they didn't have it because "it was for another customer" or whatever.  I would rather be told that it will take a week or two if that is the case.  But then I have gone back for more, a few times even. I just tack 2 weeks to what they tell me for delivery time and call every 3 days for a status on the order.  I have their poly mounts, flowmaster muffler and the SS tips.  All top notch stuff once again IMHO.  BTW I had a 2.25" exhaust custom bent and installed with the flowmaster for $200.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">      <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Howard_Sacks||12-03-2001||09:08 PM||||I've ordered a bunch of stuff from west coast fiero and have had mostly good experience.  I always ask if the stuff is in stock though and if it's not, I understand it may take a little while to get and call him everyday asking for tracking numbers;-). The quality of their stuff is always top notch and worth the cost(although I have to admit I felt a bit ripped off after receiving my $200 aluminium bushings, but they have recently lowered the price to $100 which is fair).  <P>I've had two not so good experiences. One was I asked them to include a throw out bearing when i bought a clutch and pressure plate and they didn't, but I wasn't billed for it.  It was just a pita finding someone local with one in stock.  And the other experience was I was sent the wrong part, but they made good and overnighted the correct one.<P>Neither is going to stop me from doing business with them in the future and my next major fiero purchase is probably going to be replacing my grand am brakes with their c4 upgrade.  <P>I think people don't do enough research themselves, ask the right questions or listen to what they want to hear. When I asked Chris about up and coming products or ones that are out of stock, he's been straight forward with me.<P><BR>Howard||||reg||14
Z||000015||BOILERMAKER||12-03-2001||09:46 PM||||My experience is that their product is excellent, but their shipment leaves a LOT to be desired.<P>I ordered a large quantity of stuff, was quoted 3 weeks by Eric and 9 weeks later I actually received the last amount of my stuff (with a LOT of phone calls on my part).  I also had an issue with a pricing error which Eric said he was going to take care of, but I had to call Chris and talk to him personally to get anything accomplished. <P>Chris is a good guy, IMO.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Smokin' GT||12-04-2001||01:13 AM||||Lisa, I'm getting my exhaust welded on tomorrow morning, I'll let you know how it sounds.||||reg||4
Z||000017||West Coast Fiero||12-04-2001||03:23 AM||||well, for what its worth.....<P> recently costomers may have noticed that we have switched from UPS ( Ultimate Procrastinating Shippers ) to FedEX 2 day air. <P> Mr. Van Dijk, I appologize for the clerical error on your order, but I do believe we made up for it, if we havent let us know so that we can deal with it.<P> Mr. Sachs, a pleasure as always. Thank you for stepping in with some positive input. I hope the Dogbone works well for you and let us know how we can help you in the future.<P> Mr. Nash, I do believe all I have sent to you ( 6 taillight screw covers, and a complete engine mount set ) has been free from any charge. If you have been offended by the lack of feed back from me I appologize, as there is nothing positive I have to say about your complaints on free murchandise.<P> Ms. Levine, I appologize for the length of time it took for you to receive your muffler. Your order, primarily, is the reason we no longer use the services of UPS<P> Jefrysuko, you dont like me, thats fine. You dont like my opinions, thats fine - but lets leave it at that - agreed?<P> Mr. Debrowski, I am pleased to hear that you are satisfied with our products. If there is anything else we can do to be of service let us know.<P> Mr. Hornsby, I was completely at fault for the errors in your shippment, but am pleased that everything has been address and taken care of, if the case is otherwise let me know what I can do.<P> As for any other questions or complaints, feel free to give us a call here at West Coast Fiero ( 310 ) 305-4111, or email at cwest@cwestco.com<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<p>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cliff Pennock||12-04-2001||06:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>well, for what its worth.....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon14.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||BOILERMAKER||12-04-2001||07:50 AM||||Eric,<P>I have absolutely no problems with your products whatsoever.  I tell everyone doing the 3800 that they should use West Coast Fiero products.  I have yet to put the clutch under full load yet, but will soon and will keep everyone informed on (I'm sure) how well your product is.  <P>I appreciate your appology and hold no grudges.  I was just stating facts.  You are correct in assuming that everything has been taken care of.||||reg||1
Z||000020||DRH||12-04-2001||09:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>well, for what its worth.....<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Very professional reply... As a potential future customer, this goes a long way toward removing some serious reservations I had about doing busimess with WCF.<P>Now, stay out of the pi$$ing contests!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000021||WKDFIRO||12-04-2001||10:08 AM||||I must admit when I saw the topic I put on my nomex and got ready for a fire fight. Happily, after reading the posts I will definitely be putting down the torch and simply give my impressions of West Coast Fieros for what its worth. <P>I know how difficult it can be to be in a relatively small operation. Trying to work on cars AND run a mail-order must be double tough. Ive been to West Coast Fieros many times for BBQs and for service. That means I have traveled all the way from Corona to Marina Del Rey to have them work on my Fiero. I will be using them in the future for future repairs/modifications. They have fun doing what they do there. They honestly try to do the right thing and try to make things right when they have to. <P>Somewhere in there, Eric also manages to work on Fieros West's website. He and Chris comprise Fieros West's Activities Coordinators and have been pretty resilient to our continued lack of participation.<P>In our club we have had our fair share of flakes and do-nothings. Both Chris and Eric have been the exceptions to the rule and have indeed tried to breathe some new life into the club and to the Fiero community at large.  <P>Anthony P. Sisneros<BR>President, Fieros West<P>P.S.<BR>Fierolisa, I had my 2 1/2 inch cat back mandrel bent exhaust fabricated for $250!!! That guy OBVIOUSLY doesn't want your business.<P>[ <p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000022||Jefrysuko||12-04-2001||10:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>Jefrysuko, you dont like me, thats fine. You dont like my opinions, thats fine - but lets leave it at that - agreed?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed - that is why I made no comments of my own.  I personally like many of the products you offer and liked seeing the you could behave professionally as you did here.||||reg||1
Z||000023||AkursedX||12-04-2001||11:04 AM||||Well I have never personally bought anything from WCF, although I will most likely be buying a spintech muffler sometime soon, but I have e-mailed them with questions a couple of times and they were friendly and quick to respond on them. Hopefully I will be pleased if I choose to purchase from WCF, and I really don't feel that I need to worry.  I might just have to be patient to wait for my product<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Smokin' GT||12-04-2001||12:05 PM||||Eric- Yes you did make it up, thank you very much.  I think I was a bit confused because 2 days took 4 (I think that was due to federal express's policies on weekends being workdays, hence the late delivery).<P>I definitely plan to do business with you in the future, the product looks great.  Thank you again.<P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||14
Z||000025||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-04-2001||02:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>well, for what its worth.....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon14.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000026||kevin||12-04-2001||05:49 PM||||I also bought the $200.00 aluminum cradle bushings from WCF.Great product! However thier delivery took longer than what they said and some of the peices were missing in the order. I felt personally dinged by the lower cost of $100.00. I would do business with them again.CHris is very informative.||||reg||1
Z||000027||artherd||12-04-2001||11:43 PM||||I've met Chris and Eric in the past (at a Northern CA club event) They're  Fiero-Crazy guys who have a *zillion* things to do in any one day.<P>You guys really need more employees, but as a buisness owner myself I know good help is nearly impossible to find, and good affordable help does *not* exist! :S)<P>What it boils down to is: I would NOT order a part from WCF if I needed it for my daily driver which was broken and had to get me to work the next day....<P>I *ABSOLUTELY WOULD* buy from them for my project car, OR for non-emercency replacements to ANY of my cars.<P>The quality of their product is, in my opinion, very very good.<P>If you realize that they're a small shop, and don't just have a hundred custom TIG welded battery boxes on the shelves all the time, that someone there (probally Chris) has to MAKE THE BOX from the ground up, in order to get it to you, it all makes perfect sense.<P>Thanks for making parts for our cars guys, see you next year!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000028||BlackStang95||12-05-2001||12:41 AM||||west coast fiero killed my brother!  i mean, yeah.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000029||STUK'N'80s||12-05-2001||08:03 PM||||All I have to say is that they have been a great bunch of guys out there at WCF, always enthusiastic about Fiero's, very supportive and helpfull to all us fiero owners (who usually are anal, and paranoid anyway (-:  plus their products are unrivalled and top top notch.  They have really done a number on my 85GT with their dogbone strut, air intake, strut tower brace, flowmaster muffler, to name a few mods, and they are already watering at their mouths to have their way on my newly aquired 87GT.  This is all I have to say to them....HAVE AT IT GUYS!!! and keep up the great work/service U do.||||reg||14
